{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>One language.</b> With patach when it is determinate, and if it is in construct state it comes with kamatz gadol, and in the Book of Grammar I explained why one dalet is missing. And Peleg was, as it appears, from Shem. The view is that it was two hundred years after the Flood, and he was called Peleg because in his lifetime the earth was divided, like the Aramaic translation 'half,' and similarly פלגי מים (Psalms 1:3) — these are the channels of water by which a river is divided. And so too אי כבוד (1 Samuel 4:21) and עמנואל (Isaiah 7:14), which is the prophet's son. Also the words of Seder Olam are correct, and upon it we rely, and if so, he — Abraham — was among the builders of the Tower. And do not wonder, for Noah and Shem were alive, for Shem did not die until Jacob our father was fifty years old and more. And the meaning of שפה אחת is 'one tongue,' and what seems correct to me is that it was the holy language, and the name of Adam and Eve, and Cain, also Seth and Peleg, testify." "And the meaning of דברים אחדים: because today in every language there are words that not all speakers of the language understand, and in those days the words of the wise and the foolish were few, and they are numerous, derived from the root אחד."], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {0 "I read בפתח קטן ('with small patach'); some witnesses may read differently. I have rendered the consonant name אל״ף, though the grammar here concerns the vowel beneath it. The clause 'והפלגה היתה נראת משקו' is textually difficult; I translate hyper-literally and leave it unresolved."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:44:11.885898796Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}